   "install": {
    "title": "Self-Hosting",
    "html": "<p>OpenSEO supports two self-hosting paths. Both use email and password accounts: the first visitor creates the admin account, teammates join from invitation links, and MCP clients (Claude, ChatGPT, Codex, Cursor) sign in with the same accounts.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Docker</strong> - On your own server or computer, with a prebuilt image that is ready in seconds. Works with Compose-based platforms such as Coolify, Portainer and Dokploy. See <a href=\"https://github.com/every-app/open-seo/blob/main/docs/SELF_HOSTING_DOCKER.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><code>docs/SELF_HOSTING_DOCKER.md</code></a>.<ul>\n<li>Running the older single-container image? It keeps getting updates; <a href=\"https://github.com/every-app/open-seo/blob/main/docs/SELF_HOSTING_DOCKER.md#move-from-the-old-docker-image\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">move to the new setup</a> when you are ready, data included.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> - No server to run: one deploy command puts OpenSEO on your own Cloudflare account (works on the free plan). See <a href=\"https://github.com/every-app/open-seo/blob/main/docs/SELF_HOSTING_CLOUDFLARE.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><code>docs/SELF_HOSTING_CLOUDFLARE.md</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For security-conscious setups, two advanced options replace the accounts with your own network controls:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Cloudflare Access</strong> in front of the Cloudflare deploy, so Cloudflare checks every request before it reaches OpenSEO. See <a href=\"https://github.com/every-app/open-seo/blob/main/docs/SELF_HOSTING_CLOUDFLARE.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><code>docs/SELF_HOSTING_CLOUDFLARE.md</code></a>.</li>\n<li><strong>No sign-in on Docker</strong>, behind Tailscale, a private network or your own authenticating proxy. See <a href=\"https://github.com/every-app/open-seo/blob/main/docs/SELF_HOSTING_DOCKER.md#without-sign-in-advanced\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Without sign-in</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Either way, you need a DataForSEO API key to get SEO data. See <a href=\"https://github.com/every-app/open-seo/blob/main/docs/DATAFORSEO_API_KEY.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><code>docs/DATAFORSEO_API_KEY.md</code></a>.</p>",
